From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 15:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 57/57] pthread: m68k test-and-set returns the old value

The m68k fallback for __sync_lock_test_and_set stores the new value and then
returns that new value. GCC's atomic primitive returns the previous value.

Consequently pthread_spin_lock always sees a nonzero return after setting the
lock to one and loops through sched_yield forever. Mesa hits this before any GL
or Gallium code while libstdc++ initialises std::locale through pthread_once.

Preserve and return the old value while interrupts are disabled. This restores
the semantics expected by pthread_spin_lock without changing the locking model.
---
 compiler/pthread/pthread.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/compiler/pthread/pthread.c b/compiler/pthread/pthread.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/compiler/pthread/pthread.c
+++ b/compiler/pthread/pthread.c
@@ -119,11 +119,14 @@ static int __m68k_sync_val_compare_and_swap(int *v, int o, int n)
 
 static int __m68k_sync_lock_test_and_set(int *v, int n)
 {
+    int old;
+
     Disable();
+    old = *v;
     (*v) = (n);
     Enable();
 
-    return n;
+    return old;
 }
 #undef __sync_lock_test_and_set
 #define __sync_lock_test_and_set(v, n) __m68k_sync_lock_test_and_set(v, n)
